	)
	(text "U5\nTPS1212-Q1\nVQFN-23\nVS=WHITE\nGATE->Q5/Q6 gates\nCS1+/CS1- across RSNS"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 122 102 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5504f4fb-901b-4260-b463-cbee891b83fb")
	)
	(text "PROTECTION + REVERSE BLOCK (replaces LTC7001 + INA241 + comparator):\nU5 senses main-path current across RSNS (CS1+/CS1-). On reverse current it asserts\nI_DIR (open-drain) low; glue logic pulls INP low -> GATE off -> body diodes block.\nReverse response ~6-10us (slower than a 0.75us ideal-diode controller, accepted here:\nthe slot-car controller output stage tolerates a few us of current-limited reverse).\nAlso gives I2t overcurrent (programmable breaker) + fast 5us short-circuit protection +\nbidirectional IMON + FLT diagnostics (mis-wiring protection). TI part (cost) vs ADI LTC7001."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 145 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "6e2490d0-dab7-4582-a267-e45305f63020")
	)
	(text "TWO N-CHANNEL BIDIRECTIONAL SWITCH + SMART CONTROLLER:\nQ5/Q6 in series, sources tied (common-source = TS/SRC). Drains to CTRL_BLACK_IN\nand TRACK_POS. Opposing body diodes block both directions when off; both channels\nconduct (low Rds) when on. U5 TPS1212-Q1 drives both gates from its GATE pin via an\ninternal charge pump. VS ties to WHITE (3.5-73V range) so control is alive regardless\nof BLACK voltage AND no VCC clamp is needed (unlike the retired LTC7001)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 120 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "8471df97-bbfe-4db4-a86f-c2fb5b8dc64c")
	)
	(text "PB3_SW_EN: optional MCU supervisory enable (EN/UVLO). Unused in Rev 11."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 196 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "c3551309-2d82-4e06-9c6d-5da4c88b793a")
	)
	(text "Q6\nSTL059N4S8AG\n40V 0.59mohm"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152 84 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "dc091dad-c949-4c13-9d49-1bd6bcbcb5a0")
	)
	(text "INSERTION DROP at 40A:\n2 x 0.59mohm FET (47mV) + RSNS ~0.5-0.75mohm (20-30mV) = ~67-77mV.\nHigher than the bare-FET 47mV, but now with full protection. RSNS is a\ndrop-vs-sense-accuracy knob; set I2t/SCP/OCP thresholds for trip above 40A (~50-60A).\nBONUS: a single FET cannot do reverse-block AND forward-OCP (its body diode conducts\nthe protected direction) - the back-to-back pair is why both protections work."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 15 172 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1 1)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "e37cce69-7bbb-4ef8-a05f-f3f96558b8fa")
	)
